        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          This is the final report for this experiment. Sams CF, Konstantinova I, Meehan RT. Phenotypic and functional analysis of peripheral mononuclear  cells during long duration space flight (STS-71 final research report). In: Shuttle-Mir Science Program Phase 1A Research Postflight Science Report.  Houston, TX.  Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center;  1998:1-55 - 1-60. <p>
Data contained in the report:<BR>
Percentage of Lymphocytes on Mir 18: This graph represents the relative percentage of lymphocytes in circulating peripheral mononuclear cell populations collected from Mir 18 crewmembers.  Data are expressed as a percentage of total leukocytes; each individual data bar represents an average three subjects.  Samples were collected 150 and 35 days before launch, on flight day 11 of STS-71, on landing day, and nine days after recovery. 
<P>
Percent of Granulocytes on Mir 18: This graph represents the percentage of granulocytes in circulating peripheral mononuclear cell populations collected from Mir 18 crewmembers.  Data are expressed as a percentage of the total leukocyte count; each data bar represents and average of three subjects.  Samples were collected 150 and 35 days before launch, on flight day 11 of STS-71, on landing day, and nine days after recovery. 

<P>Percent of Monocytes on Mir 18: This graph represents the percentage of monocytes in circulating peripheral mononuclear cell populations.  Data are expressed as the percentage of total leukocytes; each data bar represents an average of three subjects.  Samples were collected 150 days and 35 days before launch, on flight day 11 of STS-71, on landing day, and nine days after recovery.
<P>
Percent of Natural Killer Cells on Mir 18: This graph represents the percentage of natural killer cells in circulating peripheral mononuclear cell populations.  Cells were identified as CD16/56 positive CD3 negative cells by flow cytometry.  Data are expressed as the gated cell percentage of total lymphocytes.  Samples were collected 150 and 35 days before launch, on flight day 11 of STS-71, on landing day, and nine days after recovery. 
<P>
T-Cell Activation Response on Mir 18: This graph represents the T-cell activation response following 24 hour incubation with a lectin mitogen.  Percentage of  CD3+ cells (T-cells) expressing interleukin-2 receptors (CD25) was determined by flow cytometry.  T-cell activation was carried out on cells isolated from blood samples collected on L-35 (35 days before launch of Mir 18), FD11 (Flight Day 11), R+0 (Landing Day of STS-71), and R+9.<P>  
T-Cell Activation Response on Mir 18: This graph represents the T-cell activation response following 24 hour incubation with a lectin mitogen.  Percentage of CD3+ cells (T-cells) expressing CD69 markers was determined by flow cytometry.  T-cell activation was carried out on cells isolated from blood samples collected on L-35 (35 days before launch of Mir 18), FD11 (Flight Day 11), R+0 (Landing Day of STS-71), and R+9. <P>
        </div>

